= The random walk

The walk reported here is the site's uniform generator: 8 turns, 100,000 samples, seed 1729. Each step is one of the eighteen face turns, chosen independently of the step before it. One sample is one such sequence. It contributes one to a single bin, with no extra weight for other sequences that happen to end at the same state.

After eight turns the sample is looked up in the radius-4 ball. If the state sits at distance $d <= 4$, it is counted in bin $d$. If it is not in the ball, it is counted under $>= 5$. That bin means the distance is at least 5. It is not a measured distance, and it is not split into separate distances. God's number says every state has distance at most 20, so a sample in this bin has some distance from 5 to 20, and the walk does not say which. The six counts are the ones computed by the site's code. Added together they equal the stated sample size, 100,000.

#figure(
